  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nIs the lease of a residential unit at ₱15,000 per month subject to VAT?\n\n### Short Answer\nNo, the lease of a residential unit at ₱15,000 per month is not subject to VAT.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, landlords leasing residential units for ₱15,000 or less per month should not charge VAT on the rental payments. This exemption allows for a more affordable housing option for tenants and simplifies tax compliance for landlords, as they are not required to register as VAT taxpayers for these transactions. It is advisable for landlords to maintain proper documentation to substantiate the exemption in case of inquiries from the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
